 "method": "Tier 1: tests/peff_sequences.rs oracle_* compare every (description, peptide) pair of 23 digestWithVariants/generatePeptides/getVariantSequences cases, the proteoform-cap counts, getModifiedSequence (with its two warnings from the retained stderr) and getProcessedSequence against the retained stdout of the executed C++ Release build. Every expected value is a literal of PEFFFile_test.cpp at the pin (tier 3), including the four proteoform tables transcribed row for row; the required-key and unresolved-modification warnings are derived from PEFFFile.cpp:1493-1527 and :586 (tier 4). The one PSI-MOD term the class test resolves (MOD:00046) is authored in the test from its identifier, origin and Unimod link, not copied from PSI-MOD.obo. No Rust output is used as an expected value.",
